        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="measurement-note-text" parent="1" vertex="1" value="FAULT: remove both directions of East workload/hub peering. Do NOT remove the East forwarding-ruleset link.&lt;br&gt;OBSERVED: 15/15 East answers per OS; zero native failures. Median lookup: Windows 9.8 ms; Ubuntu 9.9 ms.&lt;br&gt;Direct queries to East inbound timed out as expected. Native Azure DNS resolution uses a different, linked service path.&lt;br&gt;East outbound and its upstream stay in the same hub. All four directional East/West peerings were restored afterward." style="fontFamily=Segoe UI;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;text;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=0;fontSize=16;fontColor=#242424;fontStyle=0;">
          <mxGeometry x="48" y="1065" width="1780" height="88" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="measurement-scope" parent="1" vertex="1" value="Timing scope: native DNS lookup duration, not fault-to-recovery time or application availability. 15 native lookups per OS per main test variant." style="fontFamily=Segoe UI;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;text;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=0;fontSize=12;fontColor=#605E5C;fontStyle=0;">
          <mxGeometry x="48" y="1173" width="1780" height="18" as="geometry" />
